        "jsCode": "// Nodes throw on non-2xx, so reaching this node means every check passed.\n// $input only carries the immediate predecessor, so pull earlier nodes by name.\nconst regions = $('Regions').first().json || {};\nconst products = $('Published products').first().json || {};\nconst regionCount = (regions.regions || []).length;\nconst productCount = (products.products || []).length;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ok: regionCount > 0 && productCount > 0,\n  checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n  regionCount,\n  productCount,\n  firstProduct: (products.products && products.products[0] && products.products[0].title) || null\n} }];"
